Pass FileZilla's two tool strings as UnicodeString, not std::wstring.

CFileZillaTools::GetClientString and CustomReason return std::wstring; the
rest of the interface between core and FileZilla, and both sides' own code,
use UnicodeString or wchar_t pointers. Built with a 2-byte wchar_t on a
platform whose C++ library assumes 4 (-fshort-wchar on Linux),
std::wstring is unusable: libstdc++ provides basic_string<wchar_t> as a
precompiled extern template for its own wchar_t, and char_traits<wchar_t>
calls the C library's 4-byte wcslen and wmemcpy -- the port's Linux build
of FtpFileSystem.cpp imported wcslen through it. The values are only built from
UnicodeString, compared with empty() and read with c_str(), so UnicodeString
is a direct replacement (IsEmpty for empty). On Windows, where wchar_t is
2 bytes throughout, behaviour is unchanged. Line counts are unchanged.

